From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 17:02:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libsec: forward-declare `bad_entry_type` in `acl.y`

`bad_entry_type` is defined `static` in the epilogue of `acl.y`, after the
final `%%`, but it is called from three grammar actions with no declaration
in scope.

That compiles under illumos' own yacc only by accident of the skeleton
layout: AT&T yacc emits the user's epilogue *before* `#include`ing the
`yaccpar` skeleton named by `-P`, so `yyparse` -- and with it the action
switch containing the calls -- lands after the definition. Any other yacc
(bison, byacc) inlines `yyparse` ahead of the epilogue, and the calls then
see an implicit declaration, which gcc rejects when the real definition
turns up:

    acl.y:162: warning: implicit declaration of function 'bad_entry_type'
    acl.y:572: error: static declaration of 'bad_entry_type' follows
                      non-static declaration

Declare it in the prologue, next to the other externs. No functional change
under illumos yacc.

Assisted-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 usr/src/lib/libsec/common/acl.y | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/usr/src/lib/libsec/common/acl.y b/usr/src/lib/libsec/common/acl.y
index d08e9266d4..3e7dfd7cc0 100644
--- a/usr/src/lib/libsec/common/acl.y
+++ b/usr/src/lib/libsec/common/acl.y
@@ -32,6 +32,8 @@ extern int yyinteractive;
 extern acl_t *yyacl;
 extern int yylex(void);
 
+static void bad_entry_type(int, char *);
+
 %}
 
 %union {
